  progression blocker found. Gearwell is an endless score attack, not a
  finite campaign. The 4K viewer downsampled its capture.
- Game/harness JavaScript syntax and CRLF-aware diff checks passed.
- Initial sandbox Edge launch failed; approved local-only outside-sandbox
  retry supplied the successful browser evidence. No runtime code changed.

Final carried critic verdicts from October 30 (not rerun on release night):
- Independent visual critic: VISUAL AAA FAIL / OURS LOSES against official
  Tetris Effect: Connected. Bounded recessed hearth and shared lighting
  improvements passed; whole-frame composition/material/radiance, broad
  smooth outer planes, schematic crane/arch, uniform blocks and local
  reward spectacle remain below the reference.
- Independent UI critic: UI AAA FAIL / OURS LOSES against the same shipped
  reference. Recovery alignment passed without a glaring readability/fit
  blocker; generic briefing, dense320 secondary hierarchy and plain
  status/leaderboard presentation remain debt.
- Recognizable identities made those side-by-side comparisons, not truly
  blind studies. Gameplay/audio/VFX AAA acceptance and an independent
  shipping judge are absent; the forced-release path does not require them.

Carried debt: authored whole-room materials/silhouette and coherent reward
spectacle; secondary UI hierarchy and briefing; direct speaker listening,
mix/latency and motion evaluation; physical-device touch, unaided human
play/fun, and real-hardware/4K performance verification. No AAA claim.

